From 8d1c7e77a524cf5bc588296a10195227c1ad2a93 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WeiguangTWK <weiguangtwk@outlook.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:50:22 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] Neko LineageOS: [PERF MODE] Add service-managed performance
 mode

Introduce a device-wide performance mode independent of charging sessions.
Run thermal transitions on a dedicated worker and expose separate request
and application states to Settings and SystemUI.

Default to disabled after a system reboot and restore the current request
after HAL restarts within the same boot. Bound reconnection attempts and
retain a warning when the thermal policy cannot be confirmed.

Show an ongoing notification describing the low-temperature burn risk,
with an action to disable the mode. Request a heads-up notification on
successful explicit activation and keep recovery updates silent.

Allow devices to opt in through config_performanceModeAvailable and
prevent the legacy fast-charge controller from competing for the backend.

Change-Id: I7377dce35a74bff6540ac36774a3c8379dffaa5c
